    <section>
      <para>Find the approximate domain of the graph below:</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Graph of the quadratic function. h(t)=5+60t−16t^2 on a coordinate plane, origin O. Horizontal axis scale 0 to 4 by 1’s, labeled “time (seconds)”. Vertical axis scale 0 to 80 by 20’s, labeled “distance above ground (feet)”. Some of the points of this function are (0 comma 5), (1 comma 49), to a maximum near (1 point 9 comma 61 point 2 5) then decreasing through (2 comma 61), (3 comma 41) and (3.8 comma 0).&#10;                    ">
